Subject: Select original object lights and projected-shadow lookup with bounded native inputs
Upstream-base: 4a9ab8151d9a74e321e52b36c95d1e157d41af60

Select the original diffuse-light, ambient-channel, static shadow projection
and LightingLookup calculations independently of the stadium/camera/effect
managers. Native typed inputs supply those services explicitly. Keep Wii scalar
records, use native matrix handles and check texture/palette capacities before
sampling. CPU palette reads decode big-endian RGB5A3; GX retains the same bytes.
Lookup ownership is transactional, and its original tint/filter formulas remain.

The decomp lacks definitions for the light tables and several constants used by
these routines. Values were verified against R4QE01 rev 1's original DOL (SHA-1
e96d2298067b70652752145b4e63644e6e1b1560, recorded in the upstream configuration):
light/mask tables at 0x804DCD00/18, projection matrix at 0x80511490, ambient colour
at 0x806DCC4C, cache sentinels at 0x806DCC70/74 and floats at 0x806E4CD0/0x806E4D20.
The scoped native cache also resets between views to handle frame-address reuse.
Zero-light ambient input is valid; six diffuse slots are the original table limit.
Skinned projection, dynamic casters and full original scene selection remain open.

